# CODEOWNERS
#
# Single-maintainer project: GitHub cannot request review from the PR author,
# so this file does not gate merges. Its job here is to WARN on high-risk paths
# -- when a PR touches one of these, the reviewer request makes the risk visible
# instead of silently merging.

# Default owner for everything.
*                       @weinotes

# High-risk: on-chain rules, scoring, and anything that decides what gets bought
# or trusted. A mistake here silently mis-scores every candidate.
/src/screener.ts        @weinotes
/src/enricher.ts        @weinotes
/src/collector.ts       @weinotes

# High-risk: credentials handling and the screening thresholds.
/config/default.yaml    @weinotes
/src/config.ts          @weinotes
/src/proxy.ts           @weinotes
/src/indexer.ts         @weinotes

# Supply chain: workflow files hold repo write access and all secrets.
/.github/workflows/     @weinotes

# Legal / attribution surface.
/LICENSE                @weinotes
/NOTICE                 @weinotes
/SECURITY.md            @weinotes
